---
title: ':beans: Green Bean Casserole (Alton Brown)'
source: https://altonbrown.com/recipes/best-ever-green-bean-casserole/
prep time: 25 minutes
cook time: 45 minutes
total time: 1 hour 10 minutes
tags:
  - side
  - vegetable
  - casserole
  - holiday
  - thanksgiving
  - make-ahead
  - alton-brown
servings: 6
---

Heat oven to 350°F with a rack in the middle.

Bring @water{3%quarts} and @kosher salt{2%Tbsp} to a boil in a large, heavy pot, such as a #Dutch oven{}. Prepare an ice bath in a #salad spinner{}. Add @fresh green beans{1%lb}(trimmed and halved) to the boiling water, return to a boil, and cook until just tender, about ~{8%minutes}. Drain the beans, then immediately transfer to the ice bath. Let sit until cool, about ~{5%minutes}, then remove the basket insert and pour out the ice water. Spin the green beans to dry them.

Pour 1 inch of @neutral oil{}(for frying) into a large heavy pot (or clean the one you used for the beans), and bring to 375°F over medium-high heat. Line a #half sheet pan{} with paper towels and set next to the cooktop.

While the oil heats, thinly slice @large onions{2} on a #mandoline{}, then combine the onions and @rice flour{1/4%cup} in a #medium bowl{} and toss to coat the slices evenly in the flour. When the oil reaches 375°F, carefully add about a quarter of the onion slices to the oil and fry, stirring occasionally, until golden brown, about ~{5%minutes}. Use a #spider strainer{} to transfer to the prepared sheet pan and season lightly with salt. Repeat with the remaining onions, then set aside.

Melt @unsalted butter{5%Tbsp} in a #12-inch cast-iron skillet{} over medium heat. When the butter is foamy, add @cremini mushrooms{16%oz}(quartered), @kosher salt{2%tsp}, and @freshly ground black pepper{1%tsp}. Cook, stirring frequently, until the mushrooms have given off all of their liquid, the liquid has evaporated, and the mushrooms have browned, about ~{10%minutes}.

Add @garlic{4%cloves}(minced) and @freshly grated nutmeg{1%tsp} and cook, stirring constantly, until aromatic, about ~{30%seconds}. Sift @all-purpose flour{1/3%cup} and @soy sauce powder{1%tsp} over the mushrooms, then continue to cook, stirring, until the rawness has been cooked out of the flour, about ~{1%minute}.

Stir in @sherry vinegar{1%Tbsp} and cook about ~{1%minute}. Slowly stir in @unsalted vegetable broth{2%cups}, scraping up any browned bits from the bottom of the skillet. Bring to a simmer, then stir in @half and half{2%cups}. Return to a simmer, then reduce the heat to low. Continue to simmer, stirring frequently, until the mixture is quite thick, about ~{12%minutes}. Remove from the heat.

Stir in the green beans and half of the fried onions, then top with the remaining onions. Transfer to the oven and bake until the sauce is bubbly around the edges and the onions are deeply browned, about ~{10%minutes}.
